## 5. Changing this schema

Adding a required section makes every existing page non-conformant the moment it lands. That is
correct behaviour, and it is also why the change is not finished when this file is edited.

Order of operations:

1. Decide the change and write down what a reader gains from the new section.
2. Update this schema and `COMPONENT-PAGE.md.template` together, in one change.
3. Migrate every existing page, or record an explicit exception per §4 for each that is not
   migrated, with an owner and a date.
4. Only then turn the check on for the new section.

<!-- DECIDE: who may approve a schema change? With dozens of pages downstream this is a decision
     with a real cost, and "anyone with commit access" is how a schema acquires eleven sections. -->

